.TH DIPIMETRICS 1 "2026-08-27" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipimetrics \- collect and serve dvbipitools metrics as Prometheus/OpenMetrics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipimetrics
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipimetrics
is a host-level metrics collector for
.BR dipitvhead (1),
.BR dipiradiohead (1),
.BR dipisds (1),
.BR dipibcg (1),
.BR dipirist (1),
.BR dipirec (1),
.BR dipidescramble (1),
.BR dipicam378 (1),
.BR dipifccret (1),
.BR dipisrt (1)
and
.BR dipixy (1).
Each of these, if started with its own
.B \-\-metrics-id
option, periodically sends a self-contained snapshot of its own counters
over a Unix datagram socket: a header (component, instance id, process
start time, sequence number, timestamp) followed by metric entries.
.B dipimetrics
retains the latest snapshot per (component, instance) pair and serves
them all as one Prometheus/OpenMetrics text document at
.B GET /metrics
over plain HTTP.
.PP
A snapshot with a sequence number not greater than the last one seen for
the same (component, instance) is dropped as stale/out of order. A
different process start time is treated as the exporter having
restarted, and is always accepted, replacing all prior state for that
instance. Malformed, oversized, or unsupported-protocol-version
datagrams are rejected outright. Up to 64 instances are tracked
concurrently; a 65th distinct (component, instance) pair is dropped and
logged under
.BR \-v .
An instance that has not sent a snapshot in
.BR \-e / \-\-expiry
seconds is dropped entirely, rather than serving an arbitrarily stale
last-known value.
.PP
The receiving socket is
.BR SOCK_DGRAM ,
bound and never blocked on: a slow or absent collector never affects
the exporters, which are already best-effort senders themselves.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-sock\ \fI<path>\fR
Unix datagram socket to receive snapshots on. Default:
.IR /run/dvbipitools/metrics.sock .
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-listen\ \fI<addr>\fR:\fI<port>\fR
HTTP listen address:port. Default:
.BR 127.0.0.1:9109
(loopback only; use e.g.
.B \-l\ 0.0.0.0:9109
to listen on all interfaces).
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-expiry\ \fI<s>\fR
Drop an instance after this many seconds without a new snapshot.
Default:
.BR 30 ,
i.e. 6 missed sends at an exporter's own default 5s
.BR \-\-metrics\-interval .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log every rejected/dropped snapshot (malformed, unsupported protocol
version, stale sequence, store full) and every HTTP 404, to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fI<when>\fR
.IR auto | always | never .
Default:
.BR auto .
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Fork to background after startup, detach from terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH HTTP ENDPOINT
.BR \-l / \-\-listen
is the address:port
.B GET /metrics
is served on. Every other path returns
.BR 404 .
The server is intentionally minimal: up to 8 connections in flight at
once, a 5-second read/write budget per connection so a stalled client
can't wedge the collector, and
.B Connection: close
on every response. This is a local diagnostics endpoint meant for
infrequent scraping, not a general-purpose web server. There is no TLS
and no authentication.
.PP
Output is
.BR application/openmetrics-text :
one
.B # TYPE
/
.B # HELP
pair per metric family actually present (families with zero live
samples are omitted). Every sample carries
.B component="tvhead|radiohead|sds|bcg|rist|rec|descramble|cam378|fccret|srt|xy"
and
.BR headend_id="<the\ exporter's\ \-\-metrics\-id>" ,
plus whatever label the metric itself carries
.RB ( reason ", " input ", " table ", " cas ", " codec ", " transport ", "
.BR peer ", " output ", " mode ).
The label is deliberately not called
.BR instance :
Prometheus assigns its own
.B instance
label per scrape target (the host:port of
.B dipimetrics
itself), which would collide with and rename an exporter-supplied
.B instance
label to
.BR exported_instance .
.PP
One extra, collector-computed series is added per tracked instance:
.BR dvbipi_metrics_snapshot_age_seconds ,
seconds since that instance's last accepted snapshot, independent of
anything the exporter itself reports.
.PP
.B dipimetrics
also reports on itself, always present regardless of what's currently
tracked:
.BR dvbipi_metrics_instances
(gauge, exporter instances currently held in the store),
.BR dvbipi_metrics_snapshots_received_total
(counter),
.BR dvbipi_metrics_snapshots_rejected_total{reason="malformed|stale|full|version"}
(counter, one series per reason),
.BR dvbipi_metrics_snapshot_entries_dropped_total
(counter, metric entries dropped from an otherwise-accepted snapshot
past its per-snapshot entry cap) and
.BR dvbipi_metrics_http_requests_total{status="200|404"}
(counter, one series per status).
.SH SIGNALS
.BR \(haC ,
SIGINT or SIGTERM stop the process: sockets are closed and the Unix
socket file is removed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipimetrics
Start the collector with defaults.
.TP
.B dipimetrics \-l 0.0.0.0:9109 \-e 60
Reachable from another host, with a longer expiry.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success.
A non-zero status is returned on argument errors or socket/bind failure.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/dvbipitools/metrics.sock
Default Unix datagram socket for receiving snapshots from exporters,
unless overridden with
.BR \-S / \-\-sock .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipitvhead (1),
.BR dipiradiohead (1),
.BR dipisds (1),
.BR dipibcg (1),
.BR dipirist (1),
.BR dipirec (1),
.BR dipidescramble (1),
.BR dipicam378 (1),
.BR dipifccret (1),
.BR dipisrt (1),
.BR dipixy (1)
.PP
